# config.oot Schema

File: docs/config_schema.oot

The config file at `~/.config/ooda-tui/config.oot` (mode 0600) holds
provider credentials and session defaults. Format is markdown-like
key=value with provider blocks.

## Top-level keys

```
provider <name>          # begin a provider block (multiple allowed)
default_provider = name  # provider used at startup
default_model    = model # model used at startup
permission_mode  = mode  # prompt | yolo | deny
compact_threshold = num  # 0.5 | 0.7 | 0.85 | 0 (off)
theme            = name  # default theme
teamwork_agents  = n     # int, default 4
teamwork_providers = [...] # list of {provider, model} maps
```

## Provider block keys

```
provider <name>
  type        = cloud | local
  key         = "..."    # required for cloud
  url         = "..."    # required for local
  models      = [name1, name2, ...]
```

## Examples

See `examples/config.oot` for full samples.

## Validation rules

- File must be readable by the user (mode 0600 enforced by writer).
- Missing required keys fail-closed with a clear error.
- Unknown keys are ignored (forward compat).
- Malformed lines exit with backup to `config.oot.bak` and a fresh
  default written.
- Provider names are unique within the file.
